                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b556398-e9fd-3f28-b4cd-f0da21fc2624",
                        "entry_id": "590203a2-8a2e-3d75-b0fd-2659de8c82f2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui a de la majesté."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f00de560-981b-48c7-99cf-0ac1bea29701",
                                "sense_id": "1b556398-e9fd-3f28-b4cd-f0da21fc2624",
                                "text": "Deux pages parurent, portant des flambeaux et éclairant une femme d’une taille imposante, d’un maintien majestueux, et surtout d’une admirable beauté."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1decca35-cc82-3dfd-831c-4238be81a1e2",
                        "entry_id": "590203a2-8a2e-3d75-b0fd-2659de8c82f2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui donne l'apparence de la majesté."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "broadly"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "959689b6-4a19-4f55-907f-34e6bc905cc1",
                                "sense_id": "1decca35-cc82-3dfd-831c-4238be81a1e2",
                                "text": "Il y a le pin d’Italie à écorce rouge avec son majestueux parasol ; il y a un cèdre âgé de deux cents ans, des saules pleureurs, un sapin du Nord, un hêtre qui le dépasse ; puis, en avant de la tourelle principale, les arbustes les plus singuliers, un if taillé qui rappelle quelque ancien jardin français détruit, des magnolias et des hortensias ; enfin, c’est les Invalides des héros de l’horticulture, tour à tour à la mode et oubliés, comme tous les héros."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8f218893-1ae8-4758-aec9-b9da3f0aa68b",
                                "sense_id": "1decca35-cc82-3dfd-831c-4238be81a1e2",
                                "text": "Je lui apportais les bonbons, les gâteaux, les oranges que dans nos représentations les enfants nous donnaient d’un air majestueux en nous disant : « Pour le chien »."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d35b0bd0-8560-4db9-8c4f-aec2c457c7eb",
                                "sense_id": "1decca35-cc82-3dfd-831c-4238be81a1e2",
                                "text": "En plein Atlantique, […], se dresse un étrange rocher, majestueux et terrible dans son isolement. […]. Rokall dresse son sommet à 21 mètres, hauteur d'une maison de cinq étages, et sa circonférence est d'environ 100 mètres."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5142b05d-549f-4115-91ac-40d50d79d97a",
                                "sense_id": "1decca35-cc82-3dfd-831c-4238be81a1e2",
                                "text": "Les montagnes s'élevant à des hauteurs majestueuses formaient une espèce de cirque, d'immense amphithéâtre naturel autour du bassin qu'était la rade."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "37448faa-5a8a-449b-860a-161f64487efe",
                                "sense_id": "1decca35-cc82-3dfd-831c-4238be81a1e2",
                                "text": "Avec Saint-Sulpice, c’est l’église la plus majestueuse que j’aie jamais vue. Saint-Pierre de Rome est plus grandiose que majestueuse. La majesté est affaire d’intériorité, d’éclat moral."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9fb7eb30-fdf8-40a4-952f-01b25f6de88b",
                                "sense_id": "1decca35-cc82-3dfd-831c-4238be81a1e2",
                                "text": "C'était une grande pièce de laine, de couleur écrue, un habit majestueux mais lourd et encombrant. La toge était jetée sur l'épaule gauche, drapée sous le bras droit, […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4b81cc8f-3f1f-4eab-9fb7-78fead819219",
                        "source_entry_id": "590203a2-8a2e-3d75-b0fd-2659de8c82f2",
                        "target_lang_word": "majestic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "majestic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b380bd4f-6cf6-3fe1-98e0-8bb677f33ee9",
                                        "entry_id": "88b2c243-cb80-3c97-b751-a954531764fa",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having qualities of splendor or royalty."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61e742b2-6406-4784-8be0-3e07285723b4",
                                                "sense_id": "b380bd4f-6cf6-3fe1-98e0-8bb677f33ee9",
                                                "text": "The gymnast performed a majestic vault."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c84e978-434b-4edb-9b9a-7bd0b4dfbee3",
                                                "sense_id": "b380bd4f-6cf6-3fe1-98e0-8bb677f33ee9",
                                                "text": "As the Indian languages are numerous, so do they greatly vary in their effect on the ear. We have the rapid Cóotoonay of the Rocky Mountains, and the stately Blackfoot of the plains, the slow embarrassed Flat-head of the mountains, the smooth-toned Pierced-nose, the guttural difficult Sússee and Chépewyán, the sing-song A'ssinneboigne, the deliberate Cree, and the sonorous majestic Chíppeway."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ac2e9d33-381d-442c-9807-3f035ad35f68",
                                                "sense_id": "b380bd4f-6cf6-3fe1-98e0-8bb677f33ee9",
                                                "text": "Equally I can stand in a station like Lucerne in Switzerland, and watch with ill-concealed admiration the majestic entry of one of the latest Gotthard \"Ae 6/6\" electrics, packing 6,000 horsepower within its 60 ft. of length and 121 tons of weight, with its sleek dark green sides and handsome stainless steel bands and front wings."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c32f1dfe-7637-45bc-a45f-5884877ee983",
                        "source_entry_id": "590203a2-8a2e-3d75-b0fd-2659de8c82f2",
                        "target_lang_word": "lordly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "lordly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "521c67cc-3bc1-3db1-94a6-3e0a4d5ec558",
                                        "entry_id": "f14913f9-d5e2-3152-bc57-a07fc89499d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Of or relating to a lord."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "18bcaae2-fb01-4eed-be67-2da2d42a2cde",
                                                "sense_id": "521c67cc-3bc1-3db1-94a6-3e0a4d5ec558",
                                                "text": "Show us your lordly might: demonstrate that you can order people and get them to obey."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "79555825-dac2-457c-a1a6-d3ffc4dafa68",
                                                "sense_id": "521c67cc-3bc1-3db1-94a6-3e0a4d5ec558",
                                                "text": "But they are the peers of the Queensland Parliament, and, having no lordly robes, must approach the Old Country model as closely as possible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4b60009a-af8a-4eba-9705-02cb2d8e09fc",
                                                "sense_id": "521c67cc-3bc1-3db1-94a6-3e0a4d5ec558",
                                                "text": "[I]n that some form of duty and sacrifice (here, participation in the 1848 Revolution and a recognition of his lordly duty) is not only beneficially character-forming but also leads ultimately to a condition which is 'sublime'."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "46b1a1c3-d4a0-421d-95bf-28e5037e0d7f",
                                                "sense_id": "521c67cc-3bc1-3db1-94a6-3e0a4d5ec558",
                                                "text": "Samson, in reply to this, says, “If you are not lordly, nor value your lordly title, as you tell me, and I trust in truth and sincerity, shall I call you a phoenix?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a8a9b377-252e-493b-b84f-69308ab1994c",
                                                "sense_id": "521c67cc-3bc1-3db1-94a6-3e0a4d5ec558",
                                                "text": "[H]e's still got his lordly habits, and more so since coming out of the war as a general.' 'A colonel, Sammy,' said Rachel. 'Same thing, good as,' said Sammy. 'Boots, of course, does wear his lordly crown with style,' said Rachel. 'Don't I know it?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "77b5315c-4b0b-3176-b49c-9b5e59254221",
                                        "entry_id": "f14913f9-d5e2-3152-bc57-a07fc89499d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Having the qualities of a lord; lordlike; noble"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c234f6d-a901-47c5-98f8-535864de9922",
                                                "sense_id": "77b5315c-4b0b-3176-b49c-9b5e59254221",
                                                "text": "Deep, indeed, / Their debt of thanks to her who first had dared / To leap the rotten pales of prejudice, / Disyoke their necks from custom, and assert / None lordlier than themselves but that which made / Woman and man."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72486ea4-d889-3433-a7a0-635a5fa0e4dd",
                                        "entry_id": "f14913f9-d5e2-3152-bc57-a07fc89499d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Appropriate for, or suitable to, a lord; glorious."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d652693-a368-423b-b272-a85389abd134",
                                                "sense_id": "72486ea4-d889-3433-a7a0-635a5fa0e4dd",
                                                "text": "He asked water, and she gaue him milke, shee brought forth butter in a lordly dish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dd60b9eb-b410-49b6-8fab-863d2fa1a61e",
                                                "sense_id": "72486ea4-d889-3433-a7a0-635a5fa0e4dd",
                                                "text": "It had also its Hall, called the Priory—an older, a larger, a more lordly abode than any Briarfield or Whinbury owned; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5208ac9-a1e0-4f97-b3b3-c15e6a3b6415",
                                                "sense_id": "72486ea4-d889-3433-a7a0-635a5fa0e4dd",
                                                "text": "The maidens gathered strength and grace / And presence, lordlier than before."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9c96473d-d6e3-4d61-8e18-022cdb31e70d",
                                                "sense_id": "72486ea4-d889-3433-a7a0-635a5fa0e4dd",
                                                "text": "There was one great tomb more lordly than all the rest."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b820b93a-78b0-4e25-9a64-c6b60c7ed933",
                                                "sense_id": "72486ea4-d889-3433-a7a0-635a5fa0e4dd",
                                                "text": "That night the whisky was unstoppered and Bradly lolled in bed, smoking, and betimes sweeping out an arm of conquest for his nobbler and taking a lordly pull at it."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9fe5fb96-d944-38f5-8a9f-6625caea3ee4",
                                        "entry_id": "f14913f9-d5e2-3152-bc57-a07fc89499d0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Proud; haughty; imperious; insolent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebd44d18-e3f0-4555-acd4-f2a71b6ac212",
                                                "sense_id": "9fe5fb96-d944-38f5-8a9f-6625caea3ee4",
                                                "text": "Lords are Lordlieſt in thir wine; […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "lordly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff607d9d-6e19-358e-81da-48e92003f5e5",
                                        "entry_id": "a76894ea-9954-31b1-afd8-00e25076d97d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In the manner of a lord. Showing command or nobility."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b238045-6253-422a-b224-7c829dd282d7",
                                                "sense_id": "ff607d9d-6e19-358e-81da-48e92003f5e5",
                                                "text": "1891, Sir Edwin Arnold, The Light of the World: Or, The Great Consummation, Book I — “Mary Magdalene”, Funk & Wagnalls, page 56,\n[…] / And Herod's painted pinnaces, ablaze / With lamps, and brazen shields and spangled slaves, / Came and went lordly at Tiberias; / […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35761e15-46a5-49c1-9dba-279f38d946da",
                                                "sense_id": "ff607d9d-6e19-358e-81da-48e92003f5e5",
                                                "text": "Look at man, then, walking lordly amidst the gigantic flora and fauna of long ago; and see if seven, eight, nine hundred years do not sit serenely on his mighty brow."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "c056e179-2434-41cf-8b0b-46691c72d6c5",
                        "source_entry_id": "590203a2-8a2e-3d75-b0fd-2659de8c82f2",
                        "target_lang_word": "majestuoso",
